---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-08/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-08/interactions.json';
import {fixtures} from '../../../../lib/equipment/15-08/solver.mjs';
const a='/equipment/15-08/',photo='https://www.augusta.edu/research/core/sabc/images/iconeus-one.jpg',ref='https://iconeus.com/products/iconeus-one/',dims='https://fliphtml5.com/smavk/ezkv/Iconeus_One_brochure_v2_%28for_release%29_SCREEN/7/';
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(v===null?'undefined':String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Iconeus One | Documentary lower cart" subtitle="" description="Inspect a closed Iconeus One lower cart and compare authored rectangular widths in a separate exhibit." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="icon"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-08/">← Equipment 15-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#icon-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">15-08 / Iconeus One / Closed documentary cart</p><h2>ICONEUS ONE</h2><p>Inspect the gray and orange lower cabinet. The separate desk compares the widths of two fixed drawings. It does not use the cabinet or show imaging data.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the lower cart</h3><div id="icon-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Rear','Desk'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button type="button" id="icon-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="icon-model" aria-label="Orbitable closed gray and orange Iconeus cart with a separate drawing-width exhibit"></canvas><p id="icon-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. Only the detached desk responds: press teal for one changed width, gray for opposite changes, or gold for a zero reference.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Compare fixed widths</h3><div class="e-fields"><label>Drawing case<select id="icon-fixture">{Object.entries(fixtures).map(([k,v])=><option value={k} selected={k==='growth'}>{v.label}</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="e-row"><button type="button" id="icon-reset">Restore example</button><button type="button" id="icon-json" class="e-run" disabled>Export JSON</button></div>
<p id="icon-status" role="status">Authored comparison · One label grows</p>
<div class="e-read"><div><b>Drawing A</b><span id="icon-A-width">100 → 110 mm</span><strong id="icon-A-relative">+10%</strong></div><div><b>Drawing B</b><span id="icon-B-width">100 → 100 mm</span><strong id="icon-B-relative">0%</strong></div></div>
<svg id="icon-chart" viewBox="0 0 346 214" role="img" aria-label="Relative widths of two pairs of original rectangles: reference gray, comparison teal">
<text x="105" y="21" fill="#426675" font-size="13">Reference</text><rect x="80" y="10" width="17" height="10" class="ref"/><text x="231" y="21" fill="#426675" font-size="13">Comparison</text><rect x="206" y="10" width="17" height="10" class="new"/>
<path d="M80 30v151M163.5 30v151M247 30v151" stroke="#a9b3ae"/>
{['A','B'].map((k,i)=><g><text x="38" y={68+i*70} fill="#294855" font-size="18">{k}</text><rect class="ref" id={'icon-'+k+'-ref'} x="80" y={48+i*70} width="167" height="15"/><rect class="new" id={'icon-'+k+'-new'} x="80" y={69+i*70} width={k==='A'?183.7:167} height="15"/><path id={'icon-'+k+'-zero'} d={`M80 ${47+i*70}v18`} stroke="#9c5443" stroke-width="3" visibility="hidden"/></g>)}
<text x="75" y="202" fill="#426675" font-size="13">0</text><text x="154" y="202" fill="#426675" font-size="13">50</text><text x="234" y="202" fill="#426675" font-size="13">100 mm</text></svg>
<p>Relative difference is 100 × (comparison − reference) ÷ reference. A zero reference makes the percentage undefined, not zero. <a href={a+'example-widths.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section></div>
<section id="icon-references"><h3>Documentary geometry</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Iconeus One lower cart with gray panels, orange accents and casters"/><figcaption>Original drawing from the <a href={photo}>Augusta University Iconeus One photograph</a>. The gray/black lower cart, orange face and side accents, beveled lid and caster stand establish the chosen generation’s appearance. No exact equipment SKU is asserted.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original cabinet and physically detached drawing desk"/><figcaption>The off-device desk and exhibit are original additions. The cabinet is sealed, with an original blank rear and no working features. The upper package in the <a href={ref}>manufacturer overview</a> is intentionally omitted.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension / feature</th><th>Reference and model treatment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published W × D × H</td><td><a href={dims}>Iconeus One brochure v2, p. 7</a>: 810 × 974 × 651 mm. The brochure does not state the dimensional datum; these values size the lower digital cart by assumption. They are not verified cabinet measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>Subassembly proportions</td><td>Photographic estimate only. The wiring, electronics, connectors, monitor, arm and other working hardware are absent.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>No animals, physical operation, images, samples, real data, or experiments enter the exhibit. The two geometric drawings are immutable authored references. The original register’s ultrasound acquisition and functional-map acceptance are not implemented.</p></section>
<section id="icon-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{show(x.expected)}</td><td>{show(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'iconeus-one-lower-cart.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives. Optional WebXR; physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#icon header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#icon h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#icon section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#icon button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#icon button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#icon-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#icon select{min-height:2.45rem;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border)}#icon .e-fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}#icon .e-read{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;margin:.6rem 0}#icon .e-read>div{display:grid;gap:.25rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.3rem 0}#icon-chart{display:block;width:min(100%,420px);height:auto;background:#edeae0}#icon-chart .ref{fill:#7c909c}#icon-chart .new{fill:#307a75}
/* Use the full touch viewport for the viewer, selector and offline exercise. */
@media (max-width: 760px) {
  #icon .e-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  #icon .e-grid > * { min-inline-size: 0; }
  #icon .e-grid figure { margin-inline: 0; }
  #icon .e-grid img { display: block; max-inline-size: 100%; height: auto; }
  #icon .e-fields :is(label,select) { min-inline-size: 0; max-inline-size: 100%; }
  #icon select { box-sizing: border-box; }
  #icon .e-over { min-inline-size: 0; max-inline-size: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
  #icon .e-over :is(th,td) { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
}
</style>


